{% if project_type == "backend" %}
## Backend Runtime

Run the backend without auto-reload:

```bash
make run
```

Run the local development server with auto-reload:

```bash
make dev
```

The FastAPI entry point is `backend/src/app/main.py` (`app.main:app`). By default the
service listens on `http://127.0.0.1:8000`; override with `HOST` and `PORT`.

| Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `GET /health` | Process health check. |
| `GET /ready` | Readiness check. Without external services, readiness means the app loaded successfully. |
| `GET /openapi.json` | OpenAPI document. |

`make build` writes a wheel and source distribution to `backend/dist/`. The wheel is
installable in a clean Python environment and can run with:

```bash
uvicorn app.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
```

This is a shared-environment baseline, not a production deployment.
{% endif %}

{% if project_type == "library" %}
## Package

Build artifacts are written to `dist/`. Verify the wheel from a clean environment:

```bash
uv venv /tmp/{{ project_slug }}-consumer
uv pip install --python /tmp/{{ project_slug }}-consumer/bin/python dist/*.whl
/tmp/{{ project_slug }}-consumer/bin/python -c "from {{ python_package }} import package_name; print(package_name())"
```

The public API is exported from `src/{{ python_package }}/__init__.py`. Publishing is not automated.
{% endif %}

